          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness reports an observation made on Saturday, July 7, 2012, at approximately 10:40 PM. He observes the silent east-west passage of several yellow-orange balls, all aligned and at equal distance from one another. The witness's description immediately evokes Thai lanterns: horizontal passage of fireballs, in groups, without noise, from east to west. In Strasbourg, a light wind was blowing from the north at 11:00 PM and from the south at 8:00 PM; it is difficult to assert that the wind was blowing from the east to Niedermodern, but it is plausible. Private parties are numerous on summer Saturday evenings, and many end with a release of Thai lanterns. The GEIPAN GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B,\" a probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
